2️⃣ this Keyword
🔹 Definition

this refers to the current object instance.

Uses
Resolve instance vs local variable conflict
Invoke current class constructor
Pass current object as parameter

Example
class Test {
    int x;
    Test(int x) {
        this.x = x;
    }
}

🎯 Interview Q&A (this)
Q1. Can we use this() and super() together?

A: ❌ No, both must be the first statement.

🔥 Tricky Question

Q: Can we use this in static method?
A: ❌ No, static belongs to class.

3️⃣ super Keyword
🔹 Definition

super refers to the parent class object.

Uses
Access parent variables
Call parent methods
Invoke parent constructor

Example
class A {
    int x = 10;
}

class B extends A {
    int x = 20;
    void show() {
        System.out.println(super.x);
    }
}

Output
10

🎯 Interview Q&A (super)
Q1. Is super mandatory in constructor?

A: ❌ No, compiler adds it automatically.

🔥 Tricky Question

Q: Can super() be called explicitly?
A: ✅ Yes, but must be first statement.

4️⃣ private Keyword
🔹 Definition

private restricts access within the same class only.

Example
class Test {
    private int x = 10;
}

🎯 Interview Q&A (private)
Q1. Can private method be overridden?

A: ❌ No (not visible to child).

🔥 Tricky Question

Q: Can constructor be private?
A: ✅ Yes (Singleton pattern).

5️⃣ static Keyword
🔹 Definition

static belongs to class, not object.

Used For
Static variables
Static methods
Static blocks
Static nested classes

Example
class Test {
    static int x = 10;
}

🎯 Interview Q&A (static)
Q1. Why main method is static?

A: JVM calls it without creating object.

🔥 Tricky Question
static {
    System.out.println("Static Block");
}


Executes before main

6️⃣ Constructors
🔹 Definition
Constructor is a special method used to initialize objects.

Types
Default Constructor
Parameterized Constructor
Copy Constructor (user-defined)

Example
class Test {
    Test() {
        System.out.println("Constructor called");
    }
}

🎯 Interview Q&A (Constructors)
Q1. Can constructor be static?
A: ❌ No

Q2. Can constructor be final?
A: ❌ No

🔥 Tricky Questions

Q: Can constructor throw exception?
A: ✅ Yes

Q: Can constructor be inherited?
A: ❌ No
